00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.670
given the changes they've already made.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:14.520
I tried to address as many, you know, non-crazy-spoilery question as possible.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.260
Double high-fives to everyone that submitted fan-subs too.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.860
Some of you had some questions about how to do that. 

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.274
So, I'll explain at the end of this video.

00:00:20.274 --> 00:00:23.770
But, just, careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:24.980
So, here we go. First question.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:25.880
Xiu asks: 

00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:30.375
"Am I the only one who doesn't trust Daario, I don't like his relationship with Daenerys."

00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:32.820
Yeah, it looks like you're not a big fan of Ed Skrein, either.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.740
I think that the new Daario is a better actor, too. Just in general.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.908
The thing about him that made me really suspicious was how quick he was to trying to get Daenerys

00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:42.374
to re-open the figting pits.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:44.763
She thinks it's barbaric and subhuman.

00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:46.995
It'll take a few more episodes to get some more evidence,

00:00:46.995 --> 00:00:50.800
but I will freaking a little bit if he starts siding with Hizdahr. 

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.794
Hizdahr, I think, is one with the agenda. But remember, Daario is a mirsinary. He can be bought.

00:00:55.794 --> 00:01:00.740
We do see him trying to defend Daenerys in the trailer here, in Daznak's Pit.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.175
So, I'm not expecting any like dramatic left-turns from the book version of Daario.

00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:09.315
I think, it's most likely, they'll just cut out some of his plot. Just because he's not gonna be on screen quite as much. 

00:01:09.315 --> 00:01:11.215
Yeah, just keep your eyes peeled on Daario. 

00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:14.154
And if you're brave enough, you can keep them peel on his butt, too.

00:01:14.154 --> 00:01:16.360
Because he's probably gonna spend most of this season naked.

00:01:16.711 --> 00:01:18.711
Next question, Dandino asks:

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.700
"Which episode is it that will outrun the books?"

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.475
So, you're asking, like, "When will the show pass the books?"

00:01:23.475 --> 00:01:25.554
I think it's gonna be different for each character.

00:01:25.554 --> 00:01:30.600
I think, Sansa will be in Wind of Winter territory this year, so she's almost already past her book story.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.671
Or even in the first episode.

00:01:32.671 --> 00:01:36.974
Bran has already caught up with his WoW storyline.  Which is why they chose to omit him.

00:01:36.974 --> 00:01:39.940
If Stannis marches for Winterfell before the end of the season

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.180
he'll have caught up with his WoW storyline too.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.255
So, that could happen in the middle of the season, it could happen at the end.

00:01:45.255 --> 00:01:50.334
Depending on how you look at the way they're changing the young Griff-Tyrion-Varys storyline

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:53.303
you could say that he's already passed his book story too.

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:58.255
But there's a lot he's doing right now, in book 5, in Dance with Dragons. So we'll see.

00:01:58.255 --> 00:02:00.300
Next question, Billtang asks:

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.380
"Do you think we'll see Melisandre's illusion magic in the TV show?"

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.050
So, you're talking about Glamour magic.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:09.435
I certainly hope we do. I mean, we've seen almost every other kind of magic.

00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:10.920
For people who haven't read the books, 

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.415
Jaqen H'ghar changing faces, the Faceless Men changing faces,

00:02:14.415 --> 00:02:16.200
isn't the same thing as Glamouring.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.540
From a visual perspective, it is.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.954
Typically, Glamouring involves the Glamoured person using some sort of charm. Like a jewel.

00:02:23.954 --> 00:02:28.134
So, Melisandre could Glamour someone, but she'd have to give them, like, one of her jewels.

00:02:28.134 --> 00:02:29.940
This kind of gets into Mance Rayder stuff. 

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:35.795
In after the episode, the creators almost unofficially confirmed that he is dead. Dead for good.

00:02:35.795 --> 00:02:41.275
So, if they do end up Glamouring anyone on the show, it's gonna be a part of a storyline that's different from the books.

00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:43.175
Next question, Ramin asks:

00:02:43.175 --> 00:02:49.451
"How could Dany ever trust Varys when he was the one giving the small council in King's Landing information about her?"

00:02:49.451 --> 00:02:52.720
I think, his meeting with her would involve an intermediary.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.694
Like, he would be introduced to her through the group that is part of the Targaryen restoration.

00:02:57.694 --> 00:03:00.180
I don't think he would just walk up to the base of the pyramid and say:

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.754
"Hello, my name is Varys, I used to sit on the Small Council. Please make me one of your advisers."

00:03:04.754 --> 00:03:08.560
So what I'm hoping is, we meet some of these other people that Varys has been

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.015
plotting and scheming with.

00:03:10.015 --> 00:03:15.274
That could be the Golden Company, they could tie the Dornish Master Plan to the Varys-Daenerys storyline.

00:03:15.274 --> 00:03:19.015
It could be Doran Martell. He could be sitting at the top of that Targaryen restoration.

00:03:19.015 --> 00:03:22.869
I don't think he's a giant fan of the Targaryens, I think he just hates the Lannisters.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.760
Next question, Liam asks:

00:03:27.156 --> 00:03:34.156
"Which character do you think they'll have to delve into WoW stuff for? I know Sansa will, but do you think there will be any major spoilers from the book in this season for other characters?"

00:03:34.156 --> 00:03:37.950
I don't know about big spoilers because the show is changing so much stuff.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.135
It depends on what you consider a spoiler.

00:03:40.135 --> 00:03:44.000
I assuming most of the people asking about WoW type stuff are book readers,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.875
who are worried that the show is going to spoil the books.

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:51.620
I'd say, at best, what the show is going to do, is just confirm a few fan theories.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.315
And the rest of the stuff will just be a dramatic departures.

00:03:54.315 --> 00:03:56.874
So, it won't even be close to what happens in the books.

00:03:56.874 --> 00:03:59.260
It's like, the book travels in a straight line,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.440
think of the show like, you know, following the line for a little bit, then going all the way around

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.975
and then coming back to, like, the point where the show ends up at.

00:04:05.975 --> 00:04:07.460
That's actually gonna be a lot of fun this season.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:13.334
Like, trying to figure out if the show confirms or does not confirm or, like, stomps on any big fan theories.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:16.495
But just remember, the show is gonna be vastly different from the books.

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:19.375
In all, but like the biggest storylines.

00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:21.020
Next question, Sariko asks:

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:27.355
"Since Brienne story line is connected to Lady Stoneheart, do you think they'll introduce us to her this season?"

00:04:27.355 --> 00:04:29.440
I'm not expecting to see Lady Stoneheart.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.718
I do think that we'll see some easter eggs for her. Like, some visual reminders.

00:04:33.718 --> 00:04:37.980
I know Michelle Fairley's name appeared on the IMDb page for the finale. 

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.540
But unless we get some more confirmation or see some more evidence, 

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.280
I'm gonna assume that a fan did that, and that it was bogus.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.280
Next question, TrueLoner asks:

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.414
"I have a question about Daenerys' dragons.

00:04:47.414 --> 00:04:51.800
Do you think they were actually trying to harm her or would they ever harm or kill her if they could?"

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.348
No, I think they were just really pissed off.

00:04:54.348 --> 00:04:56.874
Daenerys' dragons are still bonded to her.

00:04:56.874 --> 00:04:59.673
Drogon, Viserion, Rhaegal, all bonded to her.

00:04:59.673 --> 00:05:00.780
That hasn't changed.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.895
But if you cage any kind of animal, it's gonna get pissed, if you don't let it out.

00:05:04.895 --> 00:05:06.960
We have to assume that the dragons are being fed.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.180
We don't know how much and we don't know what they're being fed.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.080
So, they're probably upset about that, too.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.120
It's like you've ever owned a large dog. 

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.235
They're really sweet, but sometimes they get cranky.

00:05:16.235 --> 00:05:18.295
So, that's what I think is going on with her dragons.

00:05:18.295 --> 00:05:22.957
And if you believe that Targaryens can't be burnt by fire then she was never in any danger.

00:05:22.957 --> 00:05:25.475
Although, to be fair, they could probably chew a Targaryen in half.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.340
One of Daenerys' other big problems, in addition to her, like, people problem, is that

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.556
she doesn't know a lot about dragonlore.

00:05:31.556 --> 00:05:33.560
That's where I think Tyrion and Varys can help out.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.134
Just because they read a lot of books.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:38.099
And that's where most of the contemporary knowledge of dragons comes from.

00:05:38.099 --> 00:05:40.440
It's from old books that people wrote a long time ago.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.015
Next question, Angel asks:

00:05:42.015 --> 00:05:47.100
"What do you think about the character of Olly, the little boy from Castle Black, how do you think he'll be developed?"

