00:06:10.795 --> 00:06:12.614
Next question, Bence asks:

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:19.520
"Why did Varys say that Robert was a disaster? I though through that time, he was a mighty warrior and honorable, but why disaster?"

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.160
So, you're talking about, as a king.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.040
I think, it was just his overspending.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:26.740
Remember, it'd been almost 16 years that he'd been king.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.275
And he'd been having tournaments all that time, spending the Crown's money.

00:06:30.275 --> 00:06:32.999
Spending them into a pile of debt, with the help of Little Finger.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.780
So, he might not had been a terrible king, but he definitely hated ruling. 

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.375
The administrative part of ruling.

00:06:38.375 --> 00:06:43.775
Had someone, you know, with the mindset of Tywin been king, they might have been a little more mindful of

00:06:43.775 --> 00:06:46.380
what all the little birds of King's Landing were doing around them.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.960
Like, Little Finger's plan to destabilize the crown with crushing debt.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.000
Next question, Karen asks:

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.380
